      "body": "## Motivation\n\nA request waited for its own cache writes before returning its features. On an item whose features run to hundreds of megabytes, e.g. a Qwen3.5 video of 14k visual tokens (about 240 MB), that put the time `torch.save` takes between processing and prefill, and the concurrent misses of one prompt's samples queued on the disk together: in the TimeLens run below the engines' rollout time went up by 1.2 s per step with the cache on.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `_get_item_features` schedules each miss's write with `loop.run_in_executor` and returns; a failed write is logged. A reader that arrives before the file misses and computes the item itself, as before. `get` is still awaited, in the same thread pool.\n\n## Tests\n\n`test_mm_token_expansion.py`: a request returns with its features while a cache whose `__setitem__` blocks is still writing, and the write lands afterwards; a cache whose write raises only logs. The test helper's `asyncio.run` joins the default executor, so the other cases still see their writes.\n\nRun on the H200 devbox: `test_mm_token_expansion.py`, `test_preprocess_cache.py`, `test_model_overrides.py` pass.\n\nEnd to end: see #48305, which was measured together with this change.\n\n## Stack\n\nAfter #48286. Main port: #48306.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41768624230](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41768624230)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41768624108](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41768624108)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41768623998](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41768623998)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
